What is a database: 



A database is an organized place where data is stored so that applications can save, retrieve, update, and delete information.




Why does an application need a database?



This is the most important question.



Imagine we build a simple application:



	Browser

	   |

   	   v

	Spring Boot Application



A user creates an account.



The application receives:



Name = Vinay

Email = vinay@gmail.com



Where should the application store this information?



If we don't use a database, we could theoretically store it in memory

But what happens when the application restarts?



	Application crashes

       		↓

	Application restarts

	       ↓

	Memory is cleared

	       ↓

	User data is LOST



That's not acceptable.



Instead:



	Browser

	   |

	   v

	Application

	   |

	   v

	Database

	   |

	   +-- Vinay

	   +-- vinay@gmail.com



The database keeps the information persistently.
